                <pb facs="0304" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.13/29.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Chargé Scholle.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your telegram
                    of October 4 concerning the status of the Cuban Amnesty Bill, in which you refer
                    to the Department’s recent telegraphic instructions.</p>
                <p>In reply the Department desires to say that it is glad to know that the President
                    of Cuba has given assurances that he will veto the Amnesty Bill.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
